*metal* armor, yes. Body and especially helms. Other items such as boots
and gloves can reduce it even more. therein lies the problem from
spellcasters: low AC to survive or high AC to cast defence/attack
spells. 

The latter becomes more preferred as spell points go up, but is
absolutely not the thing to do before you reach either the mine entrance
or the Oracle (depending on your initial route of course). You *want*
your spellcaster to know how to fight competently in case he gets into
trouble with no spell points. 

You can play around with your armor and see the failure rates by hitting
"z" and then just looking at the failure rates in the right column without
actually casting a spell.

